B3.4 & Alternative Concept — Strict Priority (DiffServ EF) vs Weighted Fair Queuing (WFQ):
  - DiffServ EF (Strict Priority): Voice stays < 25 ms at all loads, slight TCP starvation only if voice >30%.
  - WFQ: Protects downloads from starvation (~70% share) at cost of ~5-15 ms extra voice jitter.
  - Verdict: Use DiffServ EF (capped via LLQ police <= 30% link) for Voice/Video + WFQ/AF for Downloads.

